---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FigLine from '../components/figures/FigLine.astro';

const bookUrl = 'https://calendar.notion.so/meet/cameronearloliver/qc3y04oud';

const record = [
  { before: '$12M', after: '$20M', label: 'Construction revenue, on a rebuilt sales process' },
  { before: '120', after: '45 days', label: 'Onboarding time, unlocking $250K in new revenue' },
  { before: '40%', after: '85%', label: 'Utilization on underused contracts' },
  { before: '50%', after: '65%', label: 'Provider utilization, on smarter scheduling' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="About Cameron Oliver | Growth Map"
  description="Cameron Oliver is an operator, not a theorist. A decade inside fast-growing companies, from employee #3 to 100+, usually the person leaders called when things broke."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <!-- HERO / INTRO -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-[1200px] flex-col items-center gap-12 md:flex-row md:gap-16">
      <div class="flex-1">
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl leading-[1.1] text-ink sm:text-5xl md:text-[48px]">
          I'm an operator, <em>not a theorist.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-[54ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
          A decade inside fast-growing companies, from employee #3 to 100+, usually the person leaders called when things started breaking.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex-shrink-0">
        <img
          src="/images/about-photo.jpeg"
          alt="Cameron Oliver"
          class="w-72 rounded-[14px] border border-hairline md:w-96"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- STORY -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline bg-parchment-deep px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[800px]">
      <p class="doc-label text-ink">How I got here</p>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink">
        <p>
          I started in project management and grew into operations. Along the way I learned to build what's called an operating model. It's basically a project plan, but for a business: how you get customers, what it takes to serve them, and the rhythm that keeps it all running.
        </p>
        <p>
          I love operations and making the thing work, mainly because I hate waste. And after a decade of it, the same pattern kept showing up everywhere I looked:
        </p>

        <div>
          {[
            'Founders making every decision themselves because nobody else had the context.',
            'Teams working hard but not on the same thing.',
            'Revenue unpredictable because nobody understood how the business actually created value.',
            'Owners carrying the anxiety of the entire company on their shoulders.',
          ].map((item) => (
            <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3.5 border-b border-dashed border-hairline py-3 text-[16px] font-medium text-ink">
              <span class="cbx">X</span>
              {item}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <p>
          Every one of those companies thought it had a revenue problem. Almost every one had an operating problem wearing a revenue costume. Growth Map exists to find that problem, and then fix it with you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TRACK RECORD -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline bg-ink px-6 py-10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px]">
      <p class="mb-6 font-mono text-[10.5px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-cream/55">What I've done</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-8 md:grid-cols-4">
        {record.map((r) => (
          <div>
            <p class="font-display text-xl leading-none text-cream md:text-[26px]">
              {r.before} <span class="text-moss">&rarr;</span> {r.after}
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 max-w-[26ch] text-[12.5px] leading-snug text-cream/70">{r.label}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHERE THIS GOES -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[800px]">
      <p class="doc-label text-ink">Where this goes</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-[1.14] text-ink md:text-[40px]">
        You don't run a factory. But your business <em>works like one.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[60ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        Whatever you sell, it's the same line. You just put your own words on the stations.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-9 overflow-x-auto rounded-[14px] border border-hairline bg-white/60 p-5 md:p-7">
        <div class="min-w-[660px]"><FigLine /></div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-[62ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink">
        Each station is a question you should be able to answer yes to. The one you can't is where the money leaks, and it's where we start.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
